Instructions to run the code:

Included with the assignment are two test harnesses that I made for myself:

harness.go:

Just spins up the server and 8 nodes, and then prints out the results (if a node is running for leader, if elected, etc.)

visharness.go:

Also spins up the server and 8 nodes but parses the output of each node to give a visualization.
Blue means follower
Yellow means candidate
Teal means leader
Red X means killed

visharness will also kill the current leader every 15 seconds, so you can see the election process start again.

alternatievly, you can just run

go run server.go

and then for i = 1...8

go run client.go i

and they should all connect the same.

tuning the 
	MinElectonWait   = 2 * time.Second
	MaxElectonWait   = 4 * time.Second
	HearbeatInterval = 500 * time.Millisecond
times in shared.go might also be nice. Just make sure heartbeats happen quick enough to
avoid nodes thinking the leader is dead.